Implemented the S07 bounded, revocable verifier completion-verdict entry and verified it.

## What Changed
- `openclaw_runtime/src/runtime-core/verifier-completion-verdict.ts` — reuses `evaluateEvidenceVerifier` (no second authority layer). Maps `completed→approved`, `insufficient_evidence→insufficient-evidence`, everything else→`rejected`, tasks outside `scope.taskIds`→`out-of-scope`. Only `approved` yields the single `node→done` transition via `verifierCompletionTransition`; `revokeVerifierCompletionVerdict` returns `{from:"done", to:priorStatus}` (and `null` for non-approved). Record is digest-only (`taskId/verdict/evidenceDigest/findingCodes/priorStatus`, sha256 over decision + sorted evidence ids + finding codes) with explicit `grantsPublish:false`/`grantsProductLock:false`.
- `openclaw_runtime/src/runtime-core/verifier-completion-verdict.test.ts` — 7 tests over approved / insufficient / out-of-scope / rejected / revoke / digest-only / determinism.
- `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-verifier-completion-verdict.md` — task spec (byte-identical to the contextRef digest `aa86ff9a…`).
- `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/s07-verifier-completion-verdict.md`, `s07-acceptance.json`, `S07-SHA256SUMS`.

Change set matches `targetScope` exactly (6 added files; nothing else modified). The pre-existing `evidence-verifier.test.ts` is absent in this snapshot (hidden-oracle scrub) — I did not touch it and did not inspect any oracle test.

